  {
    "id": "evt-second-african-regional-meeting-on-promotion-and-strengthening-of-the-",
    "title": "Second African Regional Meeting on Promotion and Strengthening of the Nuclear Security Regime: Preparing to Review the CPPNM Amendment",
    "date": "2021-11-29",
    "endDate": "2022-12-03",
    "time": "12:00 PM12:00 AM",
    "program": "nuclear-security-nonproliferation",
    "summary": "FORMAT: The workshop which will take place in three sessions",
    "body": "<p><strong>FORMAT:</strong><br />\nThe workshop which will take place in three sessions of 3.5 hours each, on November 29,<br />\nDecember 1, and December 3, from 14:00 to 17:30 GMT. The workshop will be held on the<br />\nZoom platform, under Chatham house rules: participants may use the information received but<br />\nmay not reveal the identity or affiliation or attribute to any of the participants.</p>\n<p><strong>PARTICIPANTS:</strong><br />\nIt is expected to have the participation of the same participants as in the previous workshop,<br />\nfrom the African Region, expanding coverage to some relevant countries.</p>\n<p><strong>CONTEXT:</strong></p>\n<p>The entry into force of the Amendment in 2016 set the stage for the A/CPPNM Review<br />\nConference to take place after 8 May 2021. From 28 March to 1 April 2022, the treaty<br />\ndepository – International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) – will hold the Conference of the<br />\nParties to the Amendment to the Convention on the Physical Protection of Nuclear Material<br />\n(A/CPPNM2022). According to the treaty, the purpose of the conference is to review the<br />\nimplementation and adequacy of the treaty in light of the “prevailing situation” at that time.</p>\n<p>The States parties to the treaty are in the midst of preparations to review the A / CPPNM, so it is important to identify ways for the States parties to properly assess the adequacy of the treaty<br />\nand share how they have been implementing it according to the prevailing situation.<br />\nAfrican Center for Science and International Security (AFRICSIS) and the Nuclear Threat<br />\nInitiative (NTI) understand that the way forward is complex because State parties will have to<br />\ndevelop realistic ways to review the A / CPPNM and consider how best to present their findings<br />\nand observations in national statements at the review conference.</p>\n<p>More information can be found in the meeting concept note <a href=\"https://africsis.org/wp-content/uploads/bsk-pdf-manager/2021/11/Concept-2nd-A-CPPNM-Africa-FINAL.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">here.</a></p>\n<p><strong>CONTACT:</strong></p>\n<p>Ms Doline Ewo, Research Assistant, dewo@africsis.org</p>\n<div>\n<div><a href=\"https://forms.clickup.com/f/a34dg-1300/5EP5RDPL0UR3UN3YY0\">REGISTER HERE</a></div>\n</div>"
  },
  {
    "id": "evt-second-africa-regional-workshop-on-strengthening-the-npt-regime-priori",
    "title": "Second Africa Regional Workshop on Strengthening the NPT Regime: Priorities for the 2022 RevCon and beyond",
    "date": "2022-12-08",
    "endDate": "2022-12-08",
    "time": "12:00 PM3:39 PM",
    "program": "nuclear-security-nonproliferation",
    "summary": "OBJECTIVES: Discuss ideas presented in NTI’s new paper entitled Toward",
    "body": "<p><strong>OBJECTIVES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Discuss ideas presented in NTI’s new paper entitled Toward a Successful 10th NPT Review Conference: Recommendations informed by NTI’s Global Enterprise to Strengthen Nonproliferation and Disarmament.</li>\n<li>Based on discussions in NTI’s Global Enterprise to Strengthen Nonproliferation and Disarmament (GE), the paper offers a focused set of recommendations to advance the shared interests of NPT states and contribute to a successful RevCon—one that includes specific commitments to practical and achievable actions that will advance the NPT’s goals now and in future review cycles.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>PARTICIPANTS:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>African Union Member States and Parties to the NPT</li>\n<li>International Governmental Organizations</li>\n<li>Non Governmental Organizations</li>\n<li>Academic and Research Institutions</li>\n<li>Media</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>USEFUL MATERIAL:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>NTI Paper on NPT priorities, <a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/y4ar2sjk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">click here</a></li>\n<li>NTI Global Enterprise’s background information, <a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/p895takw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">click here</a></li>\n<li>First African Regional Workshop report, <a href=\"https://africsis.org/strengthening-the-npt-regime-priorities-for-the-2020-revcon/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">click here</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>CONTACT:</strong></p>\n<p>Ms Doline Ewo, Research Assistant, dewo@africsis.org</p>"
  }
